! Cabal-Realm ~ the record

The cabal-realm law speaks at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm`>>; its dated rulings stand in that meme's <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/rulings`>>. This record keeps the history the law points to and the roads it names as owed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/history`>>

!! History

* ''The convening slip.'' The naive reading — //a Cabal IS its gatherings// — reads plausible enough that the house made the slip once already; the meme has always said the relationships define the realm.
* ''One SLOT, measured.'' Addressed alike, the realm's feed and the admission fence collapsed to ONE SLOT and each drove the other — //feeding a realm staled its own invites, and revoking an invite read as maintenance//. They now hold separate address spaces.
* ''Crucible corrections.'' The crucible corrected three over-claims in the realm model: the realm name grants no privacy (a linkability + timing surface), converge ≠ heal (the no-root-secret window), and eviction converges without finality. "Coordinator-free max-register" was right about convergence + no lockout, wrong if it meant one epoch wins free.
* ''The unswept corner's crucible'' ran as a 4-spirit swarm: Steem→Hive · Hirschman · Vitalik-legitimacy · SybilLimit · RFC-7282. The fork-as-exit build corrected the plan: a fork names a realm you LEAVE, so omission excludes the captors, cleaner than convergent-removal.
* ''The six joints.'' One word carried six entities, and different content never separated them. The wax-stamp already spoke //lineage// in its own prose, and only the type name had drifted; the doc later split into three fenced blocks.
* ''The daemon wiki on a walked hearth'' (the carry lane, 2026-11-14): a lit sibling's daemon canon and daemon working layer never opened beside another worn face.
* ''A walked browser'', joined as a face seated `write` on the hearth's `lares` workbench, painted its save with no alert and the hearth answered `not-found` — the fleet join carries no share entry and no seat (road `C15`, wave two).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ for the kahu road

* ''THE REST GATE.'' Three roads close the gap, and none stands built: wrap a workbench bag's content key for its realm's roster, seal the document under its owner's key while the owner stands lit, or rest a shared workbench under the vessel's own key. The house chose the first, the roster's wrap through the lockbox the content-key seat already runs, since that wrap alone carries to a second vessel and a second operator (road `C2`, wave two; overrulable).

<<~/ahu>>

